OL,3,ADead whale found washed up on beach in
OL,4,Astorm
OL,5,
OL,6,FPeople have been warned to keep away
OL,7,Ffrom a dead whale which has washed up
OL,8,Fon a shoreline.
OL,10,FMaryport Coastguard Rescue Team said it
OL,11,Fwas called to Flimby beach where a
OL,12,Fjuvenile northern bottlenose whale was
OL,13,Ffound on Saturday, after Storm Austen
OL,14,Fand Storm Boelo battered the UK.
OL,16,FNorthern bottlenose whales are most
OL,17,Fcommonly found in the North Atlantic
OL,18,FOcean, where they can dive to more than
OL,19,F1,400m (4,593ft) deep and stay
OL,20,Fsubmerged for up to two hours,
OL,21,Faccording to the charity Whale and
OL,22,FDolphin Conservation.
OL,23,APub: 25-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,311,300,200,140,0,100
